<title>FRANCE: No Thomson impact on Aerospatiale/DASA -minister.</title>
<headline>No Thomson impact on Aerospatiale/DASA -minister.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The expected takeover of Thomson by Lagardere does not call into question the satellite and missile links between France's Aerospatiale and Germany's Dasa, part of Daimler-Benz, French Defence Minister Charles Millon said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no question of moving towards a monopoly. The agreement between Dasa and Aerospatiale in the area of missiles and satellites will be pursued,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Some people had been suggesting that a takeover of Thomson by Lagardere would culiminate in the creation of a single European leader in the missiles field.</p>
</text>
